como precios de mercado o necesidades específicas. No se puede asumir que haya abusos sin ver la realidad completa.\nQué se puede revisar: Comprobar si los contratos [1], [2], [3] abordan necesidades similares. Ver si el adjudicatario A repite contratos en años distintos. Analizar si los contratos al límite coinciden con periodos de alta demanda.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 63 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 11.6 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 5.4, with a 95% confidence interval of 3.7 to 7.9. December accounts for 11% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 12% of all its services and supplies contracts. The contracts just under the limit are spread across 57 different awardees. Contract [1], for 14,999.99 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts in December does not indicate improper behavior. Similar distribution could result from routine scheduling. Avoiding the legal limit does not mean contracts were manipulated; it could reflect market conditions or budget constraints.\nWhat can be checked: Check the contract dates and awardees for consistency. Review contract values to ensure they align with market rates. Look for repeated purchases from the same awardee to identify patterns in spending.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["khvERJxwzgkzjChw4z%2FXvw%3D%3D","iDOLd2%2ForOPN3k3tjedSGw%3D%3D","1M7wf%2F7lgxE4NavIWzMcHA%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}